1
00:00:00,430 --> 00:00:03,870
Can you spot the two characters we can drop?

2
00:00:04,670 --> 00:00:06,510
The backticks on either side of in

3
00:00:06,510 --> 00:00:07,230
just disappear.

4
00:00:08,580 --> 00:00:12,580
The idea first came up in November 2015.

5
00:00:13,030 --> 00:00:19,110
It was implemented that December and shipped with Swift 2.2 the following March.

6
00:00:20,210 --> 00:00:23,010
Where does this function look for the value?

7
00:00:23,660 --> 00:00:25,100
In a collection.

8
00:00:25,550 --> 00:00:28,030
It searches the collection that follows the label.

9
00:00:28,480 --> 00:00:33,040
Starting with Swift 2.2, this label could be written without backticks.

10
00:00:34,140 --> 00:00:37,020
Three words were exceptions in declarations at the time.

11
00:00:37,470 --> 00:00:39,710
inout, var, let.

12
00:00:40,160 --> 00:00:46,000
They also modified parameters, so using them as labels there required backticks.
